==Distribution==
This species is native to the [[limestone]] hills and dry forest of [[Hidalgo (state)|Hidalgo]], Guanajuato, Querétaro, and San Luis Potosí states of Mexico at elevations of 550 to 2300 meters.<ref name="x435">{{cite web | last=Vallicelli | first=Valentino | title=Ferocactus glaucescens | website=LLIFLE | date=2013-08-04 | url=https://www.llifle.com/Encyclopedia/CACTI/Family/Cactaceae/1532/Ferocactus_glaucescens | access-date=2026-01-04}}{{Creative Commons text attribution notice|cc=bysa3|from this source=yes}}</ref>
